1
00:00:00,150 --> 00:00:03,381
CHAPTER 1 — CHILD OF THE STORM

2
00:00:03,731 --> 00:00:09,423
Tesla was born in 1856, in a mountain village in present-day Croatia.

3
00:00:09,623 --> 00:00:19,700
Family legend says there was a storm that night, and the midwife called him a child of the storm. His mother corrected her: no, of light.

4
00:00:19,900 --> 00:00:27,284
As a boy he saw sparks when petting his cat in the dark. His father told him it was electricity, just like lightning.

5
00:00:27,484 --> 00:00:32,946
And he could imagine a machine and run it inside his head, without ever building it.

6
00:00:33,146 --> 00:00:40,146
At university he saw a motor throwing sparks everywhere. He said you could build one without sparks.

7
00:00:40,346 --> 00:00:44,577
The professor explained to him, in front of everyone, that it was impossible.

8
00:00:45,477 --> 00:00:49,092
Tesla spent years trying to prove the opposite.
